{
  "description": "Documentaries about engineering failures and disasters: structures, loads, inspections, collapse and the investigations that follow. Research leans on official inquiry records and technical reports; graphics lean on process sequences, chronology and evidence boards.",
  "entity_handling": [
    "Never invent a failure cause, a load figure, a material property or a casualty count — if the script and retrieved sources do not state it, it does not appear.",
    "A cause stays under investigation in the telling until a retrieved source (an inquiry report, a court record, an engineering analysis) supports it; competing explanations are recorded as conflicts, never resolved silently.",
    "Technical terms from the script are kept exact — a hanger rod is not renamed a bolt, a load path is not simplified into a different mechanism.",
    "Casualty and injury figures stay exactly as the script states them; they are never rounded, merged or updated from a single secondary summary."
  ],
